   "properties": {
    "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
    "ver": "0.37.0"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 1 / 2: Extract the poses from a video (once per move)\n\nTurns a side-view video of a person into a skeleton track: a folder of keypoints, feet and ground contact that workflow 2 fits to any character. Run this once per move.\n\n1. **Load Video**: one person seen from the side, whole body in frame, static camera. Example: `example_inputs/sprint_kicks_side_720p.mp4` from the pack (\"Stationary high stepping alternating sprint kicks (side view)\" by Wellman Wellness Training, CC BY 3.0; see `example_inputs/ATTRIBUTION.md`). Copy it into `ComfyUI/input/` or upload it here. Every 2nd frame, 81 frames.\n2. **Scan Video Poses**: DWPose with the feet, about 1 s per frame on a CPU. Check *Scan overlay*.\n3. **Repair Pose Scan**: left/right label flips, lost points, flung foot points.\n4. **Track from Pose Scan**: *one-shot* (in place: kicks, punches) or *walk cycle* (+ *start*; the period is found automatically). One ground line, planted feet locked, mirrored to face right, near side = R. Check *Track preview*: orange = near limbs, blue = far, green dot = planted foot.\n**Preview Skeleton Track** plays the generated poses as an animation inside the node (frame number top left, same colours).\n5. **Save Skeleton Track** writes `ComfyUI/output/pss_tracks/sprint_kicks_v1/` (a new `_vN` every run, never overwritten). Put that folder name into workflow 2.\n\n*Save Pose Scan* keeps the slow scan, so you can cut other moves from it with **Load Pose Scan** -> Track from Pose Scan without scanning again."
   ],
   "title": "Read me"
  }
